<title>UK: Chubb gains on takeover talk.</title>
<headline>Chubb gains on takeover talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Takeover speculation pushed up shares in Chubb Security Plc on Thursday, but market makers said talk of a bid was still very vague.</p>
<p>The shares, up 33 pence at 374 pence by 0857 GMT, also gained ground on the back of a comment in the Financial Times newspaper, which highlighted Chubb's attractions to a predator, possibly from the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;It's all very nebulous at the moment,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>Chubb, which provides electronic as well as physical security services, made first half pretax profits of 46.1 million stg, at the low end of market expectations.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
